      "text": "To pull and analyze the existing infrastructure report for **Huntington Beach (HB)** from your database, you need a script that queries your BigQuery tables (or local JSON results) and filters for specific indicators of \"aging\" or \"outdated\" nodes.\n\nSince Shodan data often includes versioning and \"Last Update\" timestamps, you can use these to identify infrastructure that hasn\u0027t been patched or rotated recently.\n\nAdd this section to your **\"How to Run\"** guide:\n\n---\n\n### 📊 Generating Infrastructure Reports (Huntington Beach)\n\nThis step assumes you have already run the Shodan and Geolocation scanners and the data is sitting in your BigQuery `national_audits` dataset.\n\n#### 1. Pull Huntington Beach Summary\nTo extract all nodes associated with HB, including Shodan-enriched data:\n\n```bash\npython agent/report_generator.py --city \"Huntington Beach\" --format summary\n```\n\n#### 2. Identify Outdated/Aging Municipal Nodes\nUse the `--age` flag to filter for nodes that haven\u0027t been updated in the Shodan database for over 180 days, or that report end-of-life (EOL) software versions.\n\n```bash\npython agent/report_generator.py --city \"Huntington Beach\" --outdated --days 180\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🛠 The Report Logic (`agent/report_generator.py`)\nIf you haven\u0027t implemented the retrieval script yet, here is a Python snippet that queries your BigQuery storage to find those aging nodes:\n\n```python\nfrom google.cloud import bigquery\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef get_hb_infrastructure_report(outdated_only\u003dFalse):\n    client \u003d bigquery.Client()\n    \n    # Query to join geolocation and shodan data\n    query \u003d \"\"\"\n        SELECT \n            geo.ip, \n            geo.isp, \n            shodan.ports, \n            shodan.os, \n            shodan.last_update,\n            shodan.vulns\n        FROM `national_audits.ip_geolocation_index` geo\n        JOIN `national_audits.shodan_enrichment` shodan ON geo.ip \u003d shodan.ip\n        WHERE geo.city \u003d \u0027Huntington Beach\u0027\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    if outdated_only:\n        # Filter for nodes not updated in 6+ months or missing CVE patches\n        query +\u003d \" AND (shodan.last_update \u003c CURRENT_TIMESTAMP() - INTERVAL 180 DAY OR shodan.vulns IS NOT NULL)\"\n\n    query_job \u003d client.query(query)\n    results \u003d query_job.to_dataframe()\n    \n    return results\n\n# Example: Print report to console\nreport \u003d get_hb_infrastructure_report(outdated_only\u003dTrue)\nprint(report.to_string())\n```\n\n### 📦 Key Indicators in the Report\n*   **`last_update`:** Used to determine \"stale\" reports. If Shodan hasn\u0027t seen a change in 180+ days, the infrastructure may be unmanaged or legacy.\n*   **`os` / `version`:** Highlights nodes running outdated operating systems (e.g., Windows Server 2008/2012) that are common in municipal environments.\n*   **`vulns`:** Lists known CVEs that haven\u0027t been remediated on the identified municipal IPs.\n\n**Next Step:** Do you want the GeoJSON export logic added to this so you can visualize these outdated nodes on a map?",
